        return hashlib.md5(text.encode()).hexdigest()
    else:
        return None
```

This code snippet defines a function `string_to_md5` that takes a string `text` as input and returns its MD5 hash equivalent. The function uses the `hashlib` library to generate the hash. If the input string is empty, it returns `None`.
